  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;be a differentiable function satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Now let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Now differentiating both side we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now integrating both side we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>c</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Now given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
